{"id":"niger-delta","name":"Niger Delta gas flares","country":"Nigeria","story":"Persistent oil-field gas flares: thermal anomalies that are not vegetation fires.","places":["Rivers State","Delta State","Bayelsa"],"lang":["en"],"bbox":[5.5,4.3,7.8,6.2],"grid_deg":0.1,"data_through":"2026-11-10","built_at":"2026-11-10T16:40:47+00:00","estimand":{"primary":"Hotspots per period on the Aqua MODIS scale: the number of vegetation-fire detections Aqua MODIS would have recorded (early-afternoon and post-midnight passes). Day and night are calibrated separately and added.","why_aqua":"The early-afternoon orbit is the only one observed continuously from 2002 (Aqua) through Suomi-NPP, NOAA-20 and NOAA-21. Converting VIIRS to MODIS scale discards information and is well-posed; the reverse must invent small fires MODIS never saw, so the VIIRS-scale view is marked modelled before 2012.","secondary":["Fire cell-days (0.1° cell × UTC day with ≥1 detection), Aqua scale","Hotspots on the Suomi-NPP VIIRS scale (modelled before 2012)","Persistent heat sources (kilns, flares, industry, volcanoes) harmonized separately","Raw detections — not comparable across satellite eras"],"not":"Not burned area and not a count of fires: a detection is one hot pixel in one overpass."},"method":{"confidence_filter":"drop VIIRS 'l' and MODIS confidence < 30 (no crosswalk between the two scales); sensitivity reported","static_mask":"0.01° cells where science-quality FIRMS `type` is 1–3 for ≥50% of ≥3 detections","coverage":"share of days each satellite delivered data anywhere on Earth in each period (measured, so launches, gaps and the Suomi-NPP end come from the data); below 25% a satellite is left out, otherwise counts are divided by coverage","calibration":"ratio of totals per calendar month, day and night separately, shrunk toward the pooled ratio by empirical Bayes (shrinkage strength estimated from the data). Chain: Terra→Aqua (2002–2020, bridges 2000–2002 only), Suomi-NPP→Aqua (2012–2020, pre-drift), NOAA-20→Suomi-NPP, NOAA-21→NOAA-20; chain-closure mismatch is added to the error","combination":"inverse-variance mean of the satellites observing each period (calibration error + counting noise, evaluated at the pooled mean); intervals widened so 95% of held-out months fall inside (MODIS-denial test)","comparison":"each period vs the same month/week in other complete years: median, ratio, percentile, rank — no sigma thresholds (fire counts are skewed)","weekly":"ISO-8601 weeks; weeks use their Thursday's month calibration","provisional":"periods containing near-real-time rows are provisional: FIRMS replaces NRT with standard processing after ~3 months, and the mirror keeps only one of the two, so the NRT-to-standard difference cannot be measured from it"},"calibration":{"veg_det_D":[{"sensor":"MODIS_T","reference":"MODIS_A","window":["2002-08","2020-12"],"beta":[3.6873,8.5951,29.6346,28.1585,13.8879,7.2641,1.3846,2.0647,3.0726,3.7001,7.8039,3.8387],"pooled":7.1076,"sigma2":0.2609,"tau2":0.9488,"n_periods":218,"calibrated":true},{"sensor":"VIIRS_SNPP","reference":"MODIS_A","window":["2012-02","2020-12"],"beta":[0.1712,0.1705,0.1848,0.1547,0.155,0.1464,0.1463,0.1382,0.1362,0.1451,0.1652,0.1609],"pooled":0.1673,"sigma2":0.0964,"tau2":0.0514,"n_periods":107,"calibrated":true},{"sensor":"VIIRS_NOAA20","reference":"VIIRS_SNPP","window":["2018-05","2026-10"],"beta":[1.0063,0.9503,0.8504,0.9901,1.2147,0.9227,1.0088,0.924,1.1551,0.8243,1.0064,1.006],"pooled":0.969,"sigma2":0.0551,"tau2":0.0156,"n_periods":97,"calibrated":true},{"sensor":"VIIRS_NOAA21","reference":"VIIRS_NOAA20","window":["2024-02","2026-10"],"beta":[1.0766,0.9214,0.9745,1.1437,0.9314,1.1278,1.1007,1.1646,0.9632,1.1866,1.0136,0.9888],"pooled":1.0229,"sigma2":0.043,"tau2":0.0177,"n_periods":31,"calibrated":true}],"veg_det_N":[{"sensor":"MODIS_T","reference":"MODIS_A","window":["2002-08","2020-12"],"beta":[0.7088,0.6479,0.8267,0.7485,0.8591,0.7706,0.633,0.6313,0.668,0.7175,0.7046,0.7323],"pooled":0.7222,"s